---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>🧑‍🚀 Hello, Reader!</h1>
			<p>
				Learning, building, and thinking through code and markets.
				Welcome to Code & Trade, my personal space for learning, experimenting, and documenting my journey through <strong>coding and trading</strong>.
				I’m a self-taught programmer and market researcher with a growing interest in understanding things from first principles.
				This blog is where I write down what I learn, the problems I work on, the ideas I explore, and the lessons I discover along the way.
				I don't want to simply learn how to use tools. I want to understand **how they work, why they work, and what happens underneath them**.
			</p>

			<p>
				Coding

				My programming journey started with practical development, but over time my curiosity moved deeper into the foundations of computing.

				I’m exploring:

                * Programming and software development
                * Algorithms and data structures
                * Mathematics for computing
                * Computer architecture
                * Memory and performance
                * Programming languages
                * Compilers and how code becomes machine instructions
                * Systems programming
                * Data analysis and quantitative programming

                I enjoy taking a problem apart and understanding the smaller ideas that make it work.
                Sometimes that means writing a small program. Sometimes it means studying an algorithm.
                Sometimes it means going all the way down to memory, instructions, and the machine.
                The goal is not just to write more code, but to **understand code better**.
			</p>

			<p>
    			Trading

                Trading is another area where I’m continuously learning and experimenting.
                Markets are complex systems operating under uncertainty. There is rarely a perfect answer, so I’m interested in developing a structured way of thinking about them.

                My interests include:

                * Market structure
                * Price behaviour
                * Probability and statistics
                * Quantitative research
                * Data analysis
                * Trading systems
                * Risk management
                * Backtesting
                * Market psychology
                * Systematic decision-making

                I’m particularly interested in separating **observation from assumption** and turning ideas into rules that can be tested.
                The objective is not to predict every market movement.
                It is to develop a process that can **observe, measure, test, and improve**.
			</p>

			<p>
    			Learning

                This blog is record of my learning process.
                I don't consider myself an expert in all the subjects I write about. Some posts will explain things I've understood. Others will be questions I'm still trying to answer.
                I want to document both the **understanding and the struggle to understand**.
                There will be experiments that work, experiments that fail, ideas that change, and concepts that become clearer over time.
                That's part of learning.
                **Learn → Build → Test → Understand → Improve**
			</p>

		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
